  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 931 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge is forecast to slight shift to the west the\nbegin the week, allowing relatively (key word here) cooler \ntemperatures to settle over the TN Valley. High temperatures will \nstill be in the low 90s with overnight lows in the mid 60s to low \n70s as Moderate (level 2 of 4) heat impacts continue through the \nweek. As the ridge shifts back eastward, temperatures will \ngradually climb back into the mid 90s by the end of the week with \ndiurnal heating contributing to low chances (20% or less) of \nthunderstorm development each day. One thing to watch will be \nwhere sfc high pressure sets up along the Appalachians and whether\nor not NE AL and southern middle TN experience CAD (cold used \nloosely). If this is the case, increased PoPs may be necessary as \ndifferential heating boundaries begin to set up along North \nCentral AL. As far as heat headlines go, will likely not need \nanything past Sunday as heat indices drop to around 100 degrees.",
